(d. load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(e. unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Now origin_availability_alpha has: candidate_prepared true, origin_node_ready true, origin_node_occupied true, origin_availability_locked true, origin_availability_confirmed true, cargo_available true (since unload made cargo available). Also candidate_task_profile_linked true.)
(We also need candidate_operator_linked origin_availability_alpha? Not required for goal, but lock_origin_availability not needed. However mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready requires origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed (we have) and transport_leg_assembled and transport_leg_loading_authorized. So we don't need operator linked for origin. Good.)
(Now we need to prepare shift_candidate_beta similarly, but we also need to assign operator, skill certificate, compliance certificate, load container onto leg, stage, verify loading, establish clearance, attach service window, validate route sequence, finalize, allocate dispatch slot, dispatch.)
(We also need to allocate vehicle to shift_candidate_beta (vehicle_unit_gamma). Already have vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true.)
(We need to release compliance certificate from shift_candidate_alpha first.)
(Let's list actions for shift_candidate_beta:)
(- attach_task_profile shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, route_task_profile_available). We need vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta first. So allocate vehicle first.)
(Thus order: allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm preparedness.)
(- allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma (requires candidate_created shift_candidate_beta, not vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma). We have candidate_created, vehicle_allocated? Not yet, vehicle_available gamma true. So we can allocate.)
(- attach_task_profile shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, route_task_profile_available). After allocate, vehicle_allocated true, route_task_profile_available true (init). So we can attach.)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (requires candidate_created, vehicle_allocated, candidate_task_profile_linked, not candidate_prepared). After attach, we have candidate_task_profile_linked true, so we can confirm preparedness.)
(Now we have candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta true.)
(Now assign operator: assign_operator_resource shift_candidate_beta driver_operator_alpha (requires candidate_prepared, operator_available). We have operator_available driver_operator_alpha true. So we can assign.)
(Now assign skill certificate: assign_skill_certificate shift_candidate_beta skill_certificate_alpha (requires candidate_prepared, skill_certificate_available). We have skill_certificate_available true. So assign.)
(Now assign compliance certificate: we need to first release compliance certificate from shift_candidate_alpha, then assign to shift_candidate_beta.)
(- release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (requires candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha). We have that from init. Effect: compliance_certificate_available, not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha.)
(- assign_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, compliance_certificate_available). After release, compliance_certificate_available true. So we can assign.)
(Now we have candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_beta compliance_certificate_alpha true.)
(Now we need to assemble transport leg and load container.)
(We need origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked (we have destination locked true, origin we will lock via load_origin_payload earlier). We'll have origin_availability_locked true after load_origin_payload (step d). Good.)
(We need origin_availability_node_linked and destination_availability_node_linked (we have). We need origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (we will have origin_node_ready after activate_origin_node; destination_node_ready already true). We need origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (we will have origin_availability_confirmed after unload; destination already true). We need transport_leg_available (init true). So we can assemble transport leg using assemble_transport_leg (which requires origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available). Actually assemble_transport_leg precondition includes origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available. It does not require origin_node_occupied or destination_node_occupied. That's fine. After assemble, we get transport_leg_assembled and links.)
(Thus we need to ensure origin_node_ready true (we will have after activate_origin_node). Good.)
(Now we need to authorize transport leg loading: authorize_transport_leg_loading requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability to route_task_profile, not transport_leg_loading_authorized. We have origin_availability_locked true (after load), candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (we attached earlier). So we can authorize.)
(Now we need to load container onto leg: load_container_onto_leg requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha, candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta, loading_container_available loading_container_beta, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded. We have all after previous steps. Loading_container_beta is available (init). So we can load container onto leg, setting loading_container_loaded and loading_container_leg_linked.)
(Now we need candidate_staged_for_loading shift_candidate_beta: stage_schedule_candidate requires candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading. We have candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked true, loading_container_loaded true after load, loading_container_leg_linked true, candidate_task_profile_linked true, origin_leg_loaded? We haven't set origin_leg_loaded; we haven't done any assemble that sets origin_leg_loaded. So origin_leg_loaded is false. Good. So we can stage.)
(Now we need candidate_loading_verified shift_candidate_beta: we can use verify_loading_profile_nominal (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded). We have all; destination_leg_loaded false (we haven't set). So we can verify loading.)
(Now we need candidate_clearance_established shift_candidate_beta: we can use establish_clearance_nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). We have all; origin_leg_loaded false, destination_leg_loaded false. So we can establish clearance, which also sets route_sequence_context_set.)
(Now we need to attach service window: attach_service_window requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, service_window_available. We have service_window_alpha or beta available. Choose one.)
(Now we need to validate route sequence: validate_route_sequence requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, candidate_service_window_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_destination_availability_linked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, candidate_task_profile_linked, not route_sequence_validated. We have all after attaching service window. So we can validate.)
(Now we need to finalize candidate: we can use finalize_candidate_after_sequence_validation (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized). Effect sets candidate_finalized and dispatch_ready.)
(Thus after that, shift_candidate_beta will have candidate_finalized true, dispatch_ready true.)
(Now we need to allocate dispatch slot to shift_candidate_beta: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate shift_candidate_beta dispatch_slot_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (requires dispatch_ready shift_candidate_beta, candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha, dispatch_slot_available, not dispatch_allocated). We have dispatch_ready true after finalize, candidate_task_profile_linked true, dispatch_slot_available? Initially dispatch_slot_available true, but we may have used it for other allocations earlier. We'll need to manage.)
(We also need to allocate dispatch slot to origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha. For those, we need to use allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate? Actually that action is for candidate_entity (which includes origin_availability_alpha etc). Precondition: dispatch_ready ?candidate, candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile, dispatch_slot_available ?dispatch_slot, not dispatch_allocated ?candidate. So we need dispatch_ready for origin_availability_alpha and destination_availability_alpha. We can achieve dispatch_ready via mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready and mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready after transport leg assembled and loading authorized.)
(Thus we need to make origin_availability_alpha dispatch ready and destination_availability_alpha dispatch ready before allocating dispatch slots to them.)
(Now we also need to execute dispatch for each candidate after allocating dispatch slot. The execute actions: execute_schedule_dispatch for schedule candidates, execute_origin_dispatch for origin availability, execute_destination_dispatch for destination availability.)
(Thus overall steps:)
(- Prepare origin_availability_alpha (attach task profile, confirm prepared, activate node, load payload, unload payload).)
(- Prepare shift_candidate_beta (allocate vehicle, attach task profile, confirm prepared, assign operator, assign skill certificate, release compliance from alpha, assign compliance to beta).)
(- Assemble transport leg (requires origin_node_ready, destination_node_ready, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_available). We'll have origin_node_ready after activate_origin_node, destination_node_ready already true, origin_availability_confirmed after unload, destination_availability_confirmed already true.)
(- Authorize transport leg loading (requires transport_leg_assembled, origin_availability_locked, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability to route_task_profile). We'll have origin_availability_locked from load_origin_payload, candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability true.)
(- Load container onto leg (requires candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta, candidate_transport_leg_linked shift_candidate_beta transport_leg_alpha, candidate_loading_container_linked shift_candidate_beta loading_container_beta, loading_container_available loading_container_beta, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not loading_container_loaded). We'll have all.)
(- Stage shift_candidate_beta (requires candidate_prepared, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_loaded, loading_container_leg_linked, candidate_task_profile_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not candidate_staged_for_loading). We'll have.)
(- Verify loading profile nominal (requires candidate_staged_for_loading, candidate_skill_certificate_linked, candidate_operator_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not destination_leg_loaded). We'll have.)
(- Establish clearance nominal (requires candidate_loading_verified, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked, candidate_loading_container_linked, loading_container_leg_linked, not origin_leg_loaded, not destination_leg_loaded, not candidate_clearance_established). We'll have.)
(- Attach service window (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, service_window_available). We'll have.)
(- Validate route sequence (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_context_set, candidate_service_window_linked, candidate_origin_availability_linked, candidate_destination_availability_linked, origin_availability_confirmed, destination_availability_confirmed, candidate_task_profile_linked, not route_sequence_validated). We'll have.)
(- Finalize candidate after sequence validation shift_candidate_beta (requires candidate_clearance_established, route_sequence_validated, not candidate_finalized). Effect: candidate_finalized, dispatch)
